WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:03.330
It wouldn’t be Cyberpunk without Cybernetics.

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:09.519
Enhancing your body in the Cyberpunk universe
is both commonplace but also incredibly dangerous.

00:00:09.519 --> 00:00:14.860
A slippery slope where if you deck yourself
out too much, you risk losing your humanity.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:19.670
But this was of little concern to one cyborg
that didn’t have much humanity back when

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:23.199
they were human, and that’s who we’re
talking about today.

00:00:23.199 --> 00:00:29.320
The legendary Adam Smasher, aka the guy who
killed Johnny Silverhand.

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:34.329
When it comes to these Cyberpunk Lore videos,
we try and talk about characters and history

00:00:34.329 --> 00:00:38.090
we think might be relevant to the upcoming
video game.

00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:43.430
Adam Smasher is no exception as he’ll be
making an appearance in 2077.

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:45.300
Right there.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:51.530
So let’s take a look at the brief but important
history of Adam Smasher.

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:58.230
Adam, real name unknown, started out as a
typical street punk in New York City.

00:00:58.230 --> 00:01:04.269
Growing up in the South Bronx, Adam was the
leader of his neighborhood gang, the bloodboys.

00:01:04.269 --> 00:01:10.060
Even back then he had a nasty sadistic streak
with a dismissive attitude towards human life.

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:14.860
This would serve him well when he later joined
up with the Army, although the Army didn’t

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:21.310
see it the same way, discharging him for quote
”bad conduct and Insubordination”.

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:26.270
Adam would return to the Big Apple as a gun
for hire, or Street Samurai as he likes to

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:27.270
call it.

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:33.780
This line of work suited him until around
2015, when one day a job went south and Adam

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:39.700
was hit by several RPG-A Warheads, turning
him into a bag of meat.

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:41.610
That’s not a metaphor.

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:47.540
His friends literally shoved the chunky remains
of his body into a backpack and dragged him

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.009
back to New York.

00:01:49.009 --> 00:01:51.979
And yet Adam was not fully dead.

00:01:51.979 --> 00:01:58.000
A mysterious corporation put him on life support
as a pile of flesh only able to communicate

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.530
through a tech interface.

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:02.200
They gave him an offer.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:07.950
He could be saved, fully converted into a
metal body, in exchange for 15 years of service

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:09.110
to them.

00:02:09.110 --> 00:02:14.760
Adam accepted and was reborn as the combat
cyborg Adam Smasher.

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:20.010
This mysterious employer turned out to be
none other than the Arasaka Corporation.

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:25.950
Adam Smasher became one of their prized killers
while still given the freedom to work freelance.

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:29.420
He would take on any job as long as it fulfilled
one condition.

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:35.180
It needs to involve collateral damage and
civilian casualties.

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:39.350
Adam has long been obsessed with the idea
of being the strongest and considered himself

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:45.670
superior with his metal body, adopting the
mantra, “metal is better than meat”.

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:52.060
His need to prove his way of life led to a
rivalry with the famous solo Morgan Blackhand.

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:57.050
Morgan was the opposite of Adam in almost
every way, a professional that handled delicate

00:02:57.050 --> 00:03:01.420
situations with grace, taking his targets
in alive if possible.

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:08.000
If Adam could beat Morgan, he could prove
that metal was in fact better than meat.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:12.620
However everytime Adam challenged him, Morgan
would ignore it.

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:18.560
Eventually the Fourth Corporate War kicked
off, a bloody conflict between Arasaka and

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:19.560
Militech.

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:22.900
Adam was called in, working the front lines
for Arasaka.

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:27.600
All the while waiting for his chance to take
on Morgan who just so happened to be working

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:28.980
for Militech.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:34.390
He finally got his wish during the infamous
attack on the Night City Arasaka Tower.

00:03:34.390 --> 00:03:40.450
The details of this event are vague, a mystery
to the general public of the cyberpunk universe,

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:45.370
and books like Cyberpunk RED state that no
one really knows what went down.

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:51.140
However the adventure book Shockwave not only
details what happened but lets players participate

00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:52.140
in the event.

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:56.700
What I’m about to talk about is canonically
supposed to have happened but it's worth keeping

00:03:56.700 --> 00:04:02.340
in mind that Cyberpunk 2077 might change some
of the details.

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:07.940
Looking to end the war, Militech sent several
strike teams into Arasaka Tower, one led by

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:11.560
Morgan and another led by rockerboy Johnny
Silverhand.

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:16.630
Johnny’s team was tasked with breaking into
the Soulkiller lab, which housed a dangerous

00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:21.660
program that trapped people’s minds in a
digital prison, leaving their body an empty

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:22.750
shell.

00:04:22.750 --> 00:04:27.930
The plan went well but Johnny’s team took
a little too long and on their way out they

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:32.620
were confronted by Adam Smasher and a group
of Asasaka soldiers.

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:37.310
Pinned down in a cramped hallway by gun fire,
things were not looking good.

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:42.910
Knowing their situation was hopeless, Johnny,
SMG in hand, tried to buy his team some time

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:45.260
by taking on Adam Smasher.

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:49.240
But against Adam’s metal shell there really
wasn’t much Johnny could do.

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:54.350
Adam pulled out his auto shotgun and tore
Johnny’s body into pieces.

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:59.470
In a matter of mere seconds, the body of the
legendary Rockerboy hit the ground.

00:04:59.470 --> 00:05:01.130
Johnny was dead.

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:04.650
This sacrifice gave Johnny's team the chance
to escape.

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:09.630
Meanwhile Morgan Blackhand’s team had set
up a nuclear device inside the building and

00:05:09.630 --> 00:05:11.590
then began extraction on the rooftop.

00:05:11.590 --> 00:05:14.970
But of course it wasn’t gonna be that simple.

00:05:14.970 --> 00:05:19.510
Adam Smasher appeared, holding the mangled
remains of one of Morgan’s friends while

00:05:19.510 --> 00:05:22.460
taunting him over the death of Johnny.

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:26.520
Morgan couldn’t ignore Adam this time, and
stayed behind so the rest of his team could

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:27.780
escape.

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:33.780
There on the rooftop of Arasaka Tower, Adam
Smasher finally got his duel with Morgan Blackhand,

00:05:33.780 --> 00:05:37.950
a chance to see if metal was better than meat.

00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:40.810
Morgan’s team watched the battle from the
sky.

00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:45.900
The two were still fighting each other, even
as the nuclear detonation destroyed the tower

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:47.050
under their feet.

00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:50.080
The rivals both fell into the chaos below.

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:53.090
Their fate left unknown.

00:05:53.090 --> 00:05:56.490
But as we now know Adam Smasher did in fact
survive.

00:05:56.490 --> 00:06:00.400
We don’t know much about what he’s been
up to in the last 50 years but he still works

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:07.280
for Arasaka and has made Night City his home,
which brings us to Cyberpunk 2077.

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:11.450
Though it hasn't been confirmed, I think it's
safe to say he’s not going to be an ally

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:13.670
to protagonist V.

00:06:13.670 --> 00:06:18.800
In fact, with V on the run from Arasaka after
stealing their prototype chip, I’m hoping

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:25.120
Adam’s role is not unlike a cyborg version
of Resident Evil’s nemesis, a metal monstrosity

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:27.520
constantly hunting V down.

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:32.260
V also has the digital ghost of Johnny Silverhand
in their head who I’m sure will want some

00:06:32.260 --> 00:06:34.590
payback for their untimely death.

00:06:34.590 --> 00:06:41.520
Perhaps we’ll finally get our answer if
metal is better than meat.

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:46.090
Thank you so much for watching this episode
in our Cyberpunk lore series.

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:50.310
If you’re new I highly recommend you check
out the rest of our videos, such as the ones

00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:54.900
on Johnny Silverhand and The Fourth Corporate
War, both of which provide more information

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:58.130
on the events of the destruction of Arasaka
Tower.

00:06:58.130 --> 00:07:03.599
We have a new video up every saturday leading
up to Cyberpunk 2077's release, so we’ll

00:07:03.599 --> 00:07:04.199
see you next week.

